# İçerde — proje kuralları / project rules

- Respond to the user in Turkish and English.
- Icerde is **not** a mobile app. Ship Electron for Windows and macOS only.
- Never mix the **platform API** (Go GraphQL + MongoDB) with the **generated customer backend** (files on disk).
- Customer delivery is files (folder, zip, or git). Do **not** host customer backends in v1.
- The generated mobile stack is chosen by the user (Expo, Flutter, native, …).
- Security is X-inspired: password, 6-digit new-device code, TOTP, trusted devices, session revoke. No SMS. No phone number as identity. One active session per account.
- Every LLM call must pass the KVKK/GDPR layer (redact → model → scan → audit).
- Two LLMs: A codegen, B test/review. Switching models must change subsequent answers.
- OpenCode is the code-writing engine; do not reimplement it.
- Integrations: see docs/integrations.md. Maestro+OpenCode are runtime. Email and 6-digit codes are first-party (no AgentMail). No Figma/SMS MCP.
- Before coding a section, read its `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` and `docs/*.md`. If behavior changes, update the doc in the same change.
- Imports stay at the top of the file. No inline imports unless a circular dependency is documented.
- TypeScript switches over unions/enums must use a `never` check in `default`.
- No lorem ipsum. Real copy. Cover empty, loading, and error states in UI.
- UI is a dark workshop (ink, paper type, one brass accent). Follow docs/design-system.md and docs/motion.md. No purple AI chrome, springs, or decorative animation.
- Build order: scaffold first, then one LLM (A). See docs/build-order.md. Slice 1 (shell) is in apps/ and services/api.
